The tools used in this ethical hacking activity include Nmap and Zenmap for network scanning and reconnaissance. These tools help identify active devices, open ports, and services running on the target system. Bettercap was also used for network monitoring and security testing in a controlled environment. These tools are commonly used in ethical hacking to gather information, analyze network security, and identify possible vulnerabilities. The main purpose of using these tools is to improve system security and support defenders in strengthening their network protection.
